  m_Name: Forest_ExpertAdvice_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Game.Collectable.CollectableItem
  id: Forest_ExpertAdvice_1
  headerName: "Expert Field Notes \u2014 Surviving a Dry Landslide"
  content: "Should you face a <b><color=#C60004>dry landslide </color></b>, survival
    depends on reading the physical signs and escaping the direction of movement.\n\n1.
    Escape\n<b><color=#C60004>\tRun laterally:</color></b> If you see earth or stone
    beginning to move,  <b><color=#C60004>flee perpendicular to the slide.</color></b>
    Never run downhill in the same direction \u2014 the slide will outrun you.\n<b><color=#C60004>\tMove
    toward stable high ground: </color></b> Solid rock or a firm ridgeline is your
    destination.\n<b><color=#C60004>\tDo not shelter behind trees: </color></b>In
    a dry slide, the impact force can fell them onto you. Find a large deeply-anchored
    boulder or solid structure instead.\n\n\r2. Warning Signs\n<b><color=#C60004>\tUnusual
    sounds: </color></b> stones striking each other, the sharp cracking of branches,
    or a deep rumbling from beneath the earth like a freight train underground.\n<b><color=#C60004>\tFresh
    fissures: </color></b> new cracks appearing on the trail surface or along the
    hillside.\n<b><color=#C60004>\tDust rising from the slope without any wind: </color></b>
    That means the earth is already beginning to move.\n\n3. Safe Ground\n<b><color=#C60004>\tAvoid
    narrow gullies: :</color></b> Debris flows into low channels. Stay clear of them
    even in bright sunlight."
  type: 0
  biome: 0
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  dialogData: {fileID: 0}
